#Terraform Commands Every DevOps & SRE Engineer Should Know ⚙️

Terraform helps you automate cloud infrastructure — and mastering these commands is key to managing your infra like a pro 👇

Setup & Initialization
terraform init
Initializes Terraform, downloads required providers & sets up backend.

terraform fmt
Formats your code into standard style.

terraform validate
Checks configuration for syntax or logical errors.
Planning & Execution

terraform plan
Previews the changes before applying — safe check.

terraform apply
Applies the plan and creates/updates resources.

terraform destroy
Deletes all managed resources — use carefully!

State Management
terraform show
Displays current infrastructure from state file.

terraform state list
Lists all resources tracked by Terraform.

terraform state show <resource_name>
Shows detailed info of a specific resource.

Refresh & Output
terraform refresh
Syncs state with real-world infrastructure.

terraform output
Displays output variables from your config.
 
Workspaces
terraform workspace new dev
terraform workspace select prod
Manage multiple environments (dev, stage, prod).

Resource Handling
terraform import <type.name> <id>
Imports existing cloud resources into Terraform.

terraform taint <resource_name>
Forces recreation of a specific resource.

terraform untaint <resource_name>
Cancels the taint and keeps the existing resource.

Modules & Providers
terraform get
Downloads or updates modules used in your config.

terraform providers
Lists all providers required by your configuration.

Use terraform plan -out=tfplan and then terraform apply tfplan for safe, repeatable deployments in CI/CD pipelines.
